{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: debounce restarts its stability count on rising edges of noisy only", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-19189b08df]. Inputs: the approved RTL [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], the triage classification [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1] (unknown_failure, 30% confidence, top hypothesis likely RTL bug), and the triage reproduction [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2] (1 of 1 checks failed, $finish at 175000).\n\nDEFECT (incorrectness): the header of [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1] says a change on noisy in either direction restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches clean. The code restarts only on a rising edge (`if (noisy && !prev) cnt <= 0`). On a falling edge cnt is not cleared. Once noisy has been high long enough, cnt has saturated at STABLE-1.\n\nCAUSALITY: noisy is high long enough for clean=1 and cnt=STABLE-1. noisy then drops for 2 edges. Edge 1 has noisy!=prev, so clean holds and cnt stays at 3. Edge 2 has noisy==prev and cnt==STABLE-1, so clean<=0. A 2-edge low glitch therefore reaches clean. The specification forbids this for any pulse of 4 edges or fewer. The fault is the missed reset of cnt on the falling edge, one edge before clean changes. The cycle where clean changes is only where the failure becomes visible. In a design that restarts on any change, a level must be held for STABLE+1 edges (counting the change edge) before clean takes it, so this glitch would be filtered.\n\nRANKED HYPOTHESES, with the evidence that would refute each:\n1. rtl_bug (accepted). Refuted if the repro debounce_rc_repro.v also fails on the clean reference RTL, or if clean holds through the 2-edge low pulse on this RTL.\n2. testbench_bug (rejected). The expected value in the repro is derived again from the specification text, not from RTL output. The only checked behaviour is that clean stays 1 through a 2-edge low pulse, well inside the 'STABLE edges or fewer' bound, so the check is not at an off-by-one boundary. Inputs change on negedge, so there is no race with the sampling edge. Would be refuted by the repro failing on the clean RTL.\n3. infrastructure (rejected). [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2] shows the triage repro built, ran to $finish, and failed its own check rather than crashing or timing out. The failure follows from the RTL logic on a static reading. Would be refuted by a clean rebuild with no other change making the failure disappear.\n4. spec_ambiguity (rejected). The governing clause states 'in either direction' and 'high or low' explicitly. Would be refuted if the project specification document (not the RTL header) only required rising-edge restart.\n\nThe VeriTriage top hypothesis in [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1] was treated as one candidate only, given its 30% confidence.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX (not applied): restart on any change, i.e. `if (noisy != prev) cnt <= 0;`. Add a falling-glitch test and an assertion that clean never changes unless noisy has been stable for STABLE edges."}], "files": [{"path": "debounce_rc_repro.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: short low glitch must not reach clean", "summary": "Self-checking repro testbench for [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1] serving [requirement:req-19189b08df]. Expected values come from the specified behaviour (either-direction restart, pulses of STABLE edges or fewer filtered), not from RTL output.\n\nCheck 1: clean rises to 1 after noisy has been held high for 12 cycles.\nCheck 2: clean stays 1 through a 2-edge low pulse and its recovery.\n\nIt is meant to fail check 2 on the rise-only-restart RTL and pass on a correct debouncer. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the run nonce, then calls $finish.", "entry": "debounce_rc_repro"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001", "run:run-0002"], "claims": ["By static reading of the approved RTL, debounce_rc_repro.v is expected to report 1 passed, 1 failed on debounce_rise_only_restart.v; this has not been run by me.", "A debouncer that restarts its count on any change of noisy is expected to pass both checks of debounce_rc_repro.v; this has not been run by me.", "The specification clause used is the header comment of the approved RTL; I did not read a separate project specification document or the regression_fail.log contents."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Independent review of this analysis is still required and is not claimed. The repro gate (simulator.run, expect=fail) is run by the platform over debounce_rc_repro.v, with debounce_rc_repro as top. The repro uses only the ports clk, rst, noisy and clean, plus the STABLE parameter. It does not use internal signal names."}

